WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.700
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.635
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.703
How's everybody doing tonight?

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.538
[ Cheering and applause ]
Great to hear.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.774
In that case,
let's get to the news.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.408
During yesterday's hearing,

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:12.712
ex-Trump White House aide
Cassidy Hutchinson testified

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:16.049
that former President Trump
threw plates of food

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.484
on several occasions
when he was angry.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:19.819
Never his, of course.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.821
[ As Trump ]
Eric, give me your plate.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.889
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:26.359
After the House committee
investigating the Capitol attack

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.627
showed handwritten notes

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.729
from ex-Trump aide
Cassidy Hutchinson

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.030
during yesterday's hearing,

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.065
former President Trump
attacked Hutchinson

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.201
on his Truth social platform
and said,

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:38.371
"Bad handwriting,
that of a Whacko?"

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.672
Hers?

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.575
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yours looks like the results

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.209
of a lie detector test.

00:00:44.209 --> 00:00:45.711
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:47.780
"Sir, can you name
all the state capitals?"

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.048
[ As Trump ]
Yes.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:50.750
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.985
In a new interview,
Fox News host Brian Kilmeade

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:54.587
criticized former
President Trump

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.891
and said that he became unhinged
following the 2020 election.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.025
You know what that means --
the Fox &amp; Friends

00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:01.728
are going
to need a longer couch.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.829
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:05.531
That's right,
host Brian Kilmeade said

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.900
that former President Trump
became unhinged

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.636
following the 2020 election,
and added,

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:13.072
"I believe from the time when
the election results came in

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:15.775
until January 6th
is the worst moment

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.543
of Donald Trump's
political career."

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:19.245
And it's never a good sign

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:22.015
when your worst moment lasted
three months.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.783
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.252
According to a new report,
political strategists believe

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.020
that the upcoming
presidential primary

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.688
may push Republican candidates

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:32.091
to move further to the right
on abortion.

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:34.561
How much further can they go...?

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.430
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.899
New York Mayor Eric Adams
announced this week

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:43.570
that ratproof trash cans will be
installed around the city,

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.338
transforming New York
from a city full of rats

00:01:46.338 --> 00:01:48.441
to a city full of angry,

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.809
starving rats.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.779
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:58.151
In a new book, Supreme Court
Justice Clarence Thomas said

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.919
that Americans seem
to have lost interest

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.520
in constitutional matters,
and added,

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.156
"people tend to be more
interested in their iPhones

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:05.191
than their Constitution."

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.659
Well, I think that's because

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.227
the people who update the iPhone

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:09.395
know what they're doing.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.729
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:12.364
Texas Senator Ted Cruz

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:14.433
criticized "Sesame Street"
on Twitter yesterday

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:17.837
after Elmo promoted coronavirus
vaccines for young children.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.972
He criticized
"Sesame Street" again?

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:23.943
Dude! If you don't like
the show, stop watching it.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.011
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:27.580
You sound like me talking
about "Ozark."

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.583
"They would've been killed
so many times, by now."

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.618
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:35.087
Colorado Representative
Lauren Boebert yesterday

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:38.491
won her Republican primary,
easily defeating her opponent --

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.525
reality.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:40.726
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:42.928
And, finally,
Pinterest announced yesterday

00:02:42.928 --> 00:02:45.831
that the company's CEO will be
stepping down.

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:47.100
The announcement was made

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.968
on an adorable throw pillow.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.136
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.605
And that was the monologue,
everybody!

